SUMMARY:(509) Iolanda hides a mag 11.7 star (just outside the path)
DESCRIPTION:(509) Iolanda hides a magnitude 11.7 star\, seen from Bikaner.\
 nThe predicted edge passes 15 km to the S\, so a miss is likely — but a 
 chord from near the edge is the most valuable observation of all.\nClosest
  approach 19:25:48 IST\, give or take 1 s. The star is 15° up in the WSW 
 · dusk.\nIt fades 3.1 magnitudes for up to 1.4 s on the centre line\, and
  the path is 52 km wide\, give or take 29 km.\nFinder chart\, the map and 
 the path as KML: https://occult.alokm.com/asteroids-2026-09#2026-09-12-509
